-- MDB001: §LIVEWIRE device-mesh payloads for bim-ootb modeller/mesh.db (26 rows)
-- Implementing RESUME_DISC_WALKER_ENVELOPE_BOUND.md §LIVEWIRE — Witness: W-MESHDB-RESOLVE
--
-- Problem: the embed-8 consolidation re-keyed every geometry hash, so the 26
-- rule-carried hashes (rule_space_schedule + rule_mesh_binding) resolve 0/26 in
-- any mesh.db predating bim-ootb 670bf0f. The repaired mesh.db is LFS-tracked
-- (120MB) and the LFS bandwidth quota is exhausted until 2026-08-01 — a fresh
-- LFS fetch is not available to testers. This script carries ONLY the 26 new
-- rows (13 DeviceLibrary_residential device meshes projected from
-- component_library.db via scripts/project_device_meshes_to_meshdb.py, 13
-- TerminalMerged_rules binding meshes from Terminal_library.db), byte-verbatim
-- as hex literals, so an existing stale local copy can be brought current
-- WITHOUT any LFS traffic.
--
-- Apply:      sqlite3 ~/bim-ootb/modeller/mesh.db < migration/MDB001_livewire_device_meshes.sql
-- Verify:     node scripts/witness_meshdb_resolve.js ~/bim-ootb/modeller/mesh.db   (expect 5/5)
-- Idempotent: INSERT OR IGNORE — safe to re-run, no-op on an already-current mesh.db.
-- Target DB:  bim-ootb modeller/mesh.db (table component_geometries) — NOT a bim-compiler DB.

